&lt;h1 id=&#34;who-are-we-what-do-we-do&#34;&gt;Who are we? What do we do?
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Grutto Archeologie is a (fictional) archaeological prospection company run by NyAnna Beeman and Shelene Low. Inspired by the Grutto (Black-tailed godwit), the threatened national bird of the Netherlands, we aim to use predictive modelling as a method to help with preserving archaeology in the Netherlands which can be threatened by various development and construction projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;technical-stuff&#34;&gt;Technical stuff
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This blog is made possible with RStudio and the Blogdown R package. The blog makes use of a free &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/CaiJimmy/hugo-theme-stack&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Hugo theme from Jimmy Cai&lt;/a&gt;. Updates of the blog are continuously deployed through GitHub and the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/shelenel/grutto-archeologie&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;source code is publicly available&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
